            <div xml:id="d353">

                <pb facs="0421" n="407" sameAs="frus:frus1943v06/pg407"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.3312/431</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Messersmith</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 11656</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-07-20">July 20, 1943</date>.<lb/>[Received July
                        26.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Supplementing the Embassy’s despatch No.
                    9498 of April 20, 1943,<anchor n="10" xml:id="d353-f1"/> respecting the
                    possibility of American warships being granted the privilege of obtaining ship
                    supplies free of duty from bonded warehouses in Mexico, I have the honor to
                    transmit herewith a copy and translation of a note dated July 10, 1943<anchor
                        n="10" xml:id="d353-f2"/> from the Foreign Office, which is
                    self-explanatory. It will be noted that instructions have been issued to the
                    competent Mexican customs authorities to permit United States war vessels to
                    obtain duty-free supplies and that such ships may likewise despatch into bonded
                    warehouses all sorts of war supplies for subsequent use without the payment of
                    any charges.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Ambassador:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sidney E.
                            O’Donoghue</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Second Secretary of
                        Embassy</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
